First: what do we mean by “buttons” (important)

There are two different kinds of buttons people talk about in crypto, and they are not the same.

1️⃣ On-chain “buttons” (smart contract functions)

These are:
	•	Functions inside the smart contract
	•	Example: enableAutoHarvest(), disableRouting()
	•	They exist on Ethereum, not on your phone UI

MetaMask can call them, but it does NOT automatically show them as big labeled buttons.

⸻

2️⃣ UI buttons (dashboard / app)

These are:
	•	A website or dashboard
	•	Actual clickable buttons with labels
	•	They call the on-chain functions for you

👉 Without a dashboard, you still have the buttons, but you access them through:
	•	MetaMask → “Interact with contract”
	•	Etherscan → “Write Contract”
	•	A simple GitHub-hosted webpage

⸻

So will these buttons “show up in MetaMask automatically?”

❌ No — not automatically like a bank app

✅ Yes — they are still usable and safe

MetaMask today:
	•	Lets you sign transactions
	•	But does not render custom strategy buttons nicely yet

That’s why most serious users do this in stages.

